{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>He shall bring it for a witness.</b> The Sages already stated (Sotah 2b): wherever \"witness\" is said, two are meant. And if so, <b>whether it be torn in pieces</b> — by a harmful beast whose tearing presumptively has a witness, for upon such a beast many shepherds are called — then he shall bring the torn carcass and a pair of witnesses who will testify that this one was torn under duress." "<b>The torn carcass.</b> Under duress." "<b>He shall not make restitution.</b> But if animals consumed it due to lack of proper guarding, he shall make restitution, as they said of blessed memory (Bava Metzia 93a): a single wolf is not duress, a single dog is not duress — and needless to say a cat, a marten, and the like, which he could have driven off."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase שֶׁסְּתָמָהּ יֵשׁ רוֹאֶה is read as 'whose tearing (סתמו of הטריפה) has a witness' — i.e., the act is presumptively observable, unlike theft, which is clandestine."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:48.418123671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}